side entry left
side File(spend.toml) left
side Disk(path) left
side Web left
side SQLite(expenses) both        # import writes it, report reads and uses it: arms of one choice; the count after is no use
side SQLite(rates) both           # rates writes it, report reads and uses it
side Global(spend.rates.LATEST) right          # run reads back what it left there: closed, the place keeps what run leaves
side File(reports/report.md) right
side open right
side Screen right

# ---- what Atlas has and should not ----
# a value one arm of the choice makes, and only that arm takes, has the choice's moment
# the parameter of a sum type is not the value its call is handed: it comes from beyond
# the name a chain's last operation gives is given to every call in the chain
# an environment variable with a fallback puts the read of the variable in a choice, though it always runs
# an own arrow takes what only a step inside it takes; a result that only a step takes is no result handed back

# ---- each loop is a step: it takes what it runs over and makes the element (#103) ----
step main/?1/run/?1/Store.save/for e in expenses
step main/?1/run/?1/write/for (date, description, amount, currency) in store.rows()
